-- This recipe holds a project to the words it has decided on. The project
-- keeps a file of them, and the recipe reports each identifier and comment
-- in its .roc files that uses a word the file retires. The word lists belong
-- to the project, so none is built in here. It is written in Roc, the app
-- cookbook/roc/find_retired_words/find_retired_words.roc, the modules beside it
-- (Retired, the checks; Identifiers and Words, what they read; SelfTest) and
-- the cookbook's Roc library (cookbook/roc/lib/: Tree, Text and Finding), on
-- Shale's Roc platform (roc_platform/README.md); this file is its launcher,
-- so it is launched as every Shale recipe is:
--
--   cd <repo> && shale <shale>/cookbook/roc/find_retired_words.shale words=vocabulary.txt
--   shale cookbook:roc/find_retired_words.shale self_test=1
--
-- The arguments:
--   glob       the files to check, `**/*.roc` by default;
--   words      the project's file of decided words, which must be given;
--   self_test  with `self_test=1`, check the plants in
--              `cookbook/roc/plants/find_retired_words/`.
--
-- Each line of the words file is `kept: retired, retired`, in lower case,
-- such as `lean: tilt`. A blank line or one starting with `#` is skipped.
-- The file is matched by whole words, so a plural that should go needs its
-- own entry, and a word with a good second meaning can't be listed at all.
-- A malformed line stops the run, as does a word retired twice or a word
-- both kept and retired.
--
-- Identifiers are read from the tree of Roc's own parser and split into words
-- at underscores and capitals, so `TiltStep` and `tilt_step` both hold
-- `tilt`. They include the names a header or an import exposes, a `where`
-- clause's methods and an `as` pattern's name. Comments are read as words
-- too, and the text of a string doesn't count. There are two checks, one for
-- each place a word can be:
--
--   retired_name     an identifier that holds a retired word;
--   retired_comment  a comment that holds one.
--
-- The output is the counts, one line per finding,
-- `path:line: retired_name: tilt_step: tilt is lean here`, and the counts
-- again (cookbook/findings.shale). Each word is reported once a line for
-- each name that holds it. The run fails if there are findings, or if any
-- file doesn't parse, and the files that do parse are judged either way.
--
-- **The launcher** hands every value it is given to roc_platform/run.shale in
-- the checkout this cookbook is in (the `cookbook` mount's parent), which
-- builds the Roc there (cached; the first build after a change to C Shale
-- compiles the platform's host, 25 to 50 s) and runs the program rooted
-- here, so `glob=` and `words=` are this root's paths, as they were the Shale
-- recipe's. A value the Roc script reads no `Shale.arg!` of stops the run
-- before anything is built. Its output is the program's, then the launchers'
-- own stops when it stops. `reads=inputs` builds and runs nothing, and prints
-- the real path of each file the program is built from, one a line
-- (run.shale's header), for a caller's cache key. It is built with
-- `opt=speed`: Roc's dev build took 5.0 s of CPU over roc-apps (a words
-- file retiring common words, 5,523 findings) where the Shale original took
-- 3.7 s, and the speed build takes 2.1 s, for about 14 s of build once, then
-- cached. Its goldens, the Shale original's output on
-- the plants, are held by cookbook/roc/find_retired_words/check_goldens.shale.
-- budget: programs=10 output_bytes=8000000

const SCRIPT = "cookbook/roc/find_retired_words/find_retired_words.roc"
const CHECKOUT = dirname(dirname(real("cookbook:README.md")))
const HERE = real(".")

-- `self_test` is read here by name, as the cookbook's full tier finds the
-- recipes it runs `self_test=1` of. `arg_names()` is every value given; the
-- rest are read by a name made as the run goes, so Shale's own check cannot
-- see them: run.shale holds them to the script's reads.
const SELF_TEST = arg("self_test", "")
local values = {"script=" .. SCRIPT, "in=" .. HERE}
if SELF_TEST ~= "" then push(values, "self_test=" .. SELF_TEST) end
for name in arg_names() do
  if name ~= "self_test" then push(values, name .. "=" .. arg(name, "")) end
end
local r = run({"shale", "--root", CHECKOUT, CHECKOUT .. "/roc_platform/run.shale", "--args-stdin"}, {stdin = join(values, "\n") .. "\n", timeout_ms = 1800000, whole = 8000000})
print(trim_end(r.out))
if r.code ~= 0 then fail("find_retired_words: the Roc program stopped (exit " .. r.code .. ")") end
